Again, one of the things I've always said is that you look at subjective data when you're looking at

00:01:58,810 --> 00:02:04,650
whether my cancer is getting worse or better, and one of the most common things that you're going to see

00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:12,170
subjectively with cancer, besides possibly pain, but many times many cancers don't produce pain.

00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:20,250
That would be more in like colorectal cancer, or pancreatic cancer, or maybe prostate cancer,

00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:33,210
but more so would be fatigue. If your fatigue is long-lasting fatigue, that can be a clue that

00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:42,170
your cancer could be worsening. Why would a person with cancer get fatigue? It's not just

00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:50,650
magically you get tired because your cancer is growing. If the cancer is growing, it can cause

00:02:50,650 --> 00:03:00,650
anemia, and therefore give you fatigue. Unless your cancer is on your adrenal glands, or affecting

00:03:00,730 --> 00:03:04,810
